== The Silent Bell

Every morning, Mateo walked to the harbor with his grandfather to watch the fishing boats come home. At the end of the dock hung an old brass bell, and it always rang to welcome the sailors back. But on Monday, the bell was silent.

"Someone has stolen it!" Mateo gasped. His grandfather only smiled. "Maybe," he said. "Or maybe there is a good reason. Look closely before you decide."

Mateo crouched beside the empty post. A few muddy footprints, small ones with zigzag patterns, led away across the dock. He followed them past the fish market and up to the old net shed. The door was open just a crack, and he could hear a quiet scraping sound inside.

Mateo peeked in. His friend Lina was kneeling on the floor next to the bell, twisting a thick new rope through its handle.

"The storm last night shook everything," Lina explained without looking up. "I saw that the old rope was frayed. I was afraid the bell would fall on someone's head, so I took it down to fix it."

Mateo felt his cheeks turn warm. "I thought you were a thief," he admitted. "I'm sorry."

Lina laughed. "Help me carry it back, and we'll call it even." Together they hung the bell on its post, tugging the rope until the knot was tight. Then Mateo gave the bell a gentle pull. Its deep, clear ring rolled across the water just as the first fishing boat appeared.

